**1. Summary of the attached PDF (2015 and 2017 papers):**

The research investigates Nano-11, a dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle derived from sweet corn, as a vaccine adjuvant. Nano-11, with its positive charge and 70-80 nm size, efficiently adsorbs and delivers antigens to dendritic cells (DCs). It activates DCs by increasing costimulatory molecule expression and inducing pro-inflammatory cytokines like IL-1β and IL-12p40. In vivo, Nano-11 enhances antigen-specific antibody responses, causes transient, localized inflammation with macrophage recruitment, and targets antigens to migratory DCs in draining lymph nodes, demonstrating its efficacy and favorable safety profile as a next-generation adjuvant.

